<title>USA: Prodi sees no social reforms without union pact.</title>
<headline>Prodi sees no social reforms without union pact.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi said there could be no changes in the social welfare system without an agreement with Italy's unions.</p>
<p>&quot;There can be no changes in social welfare without an agreement with the unions,&quot; Prodi told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;In Italy the social welfare system has a major role,&quot; he said. &quot;If we had been in Britain or the United States we would have had social welfare reform last year.&quot;</p>
<p>Prodi, here for the Group of Seven industrial countries' leadership meeting, stressed that a recent government paper on social welfare reform was only the basis for discussion.</p>
</text>
